# Stablecoins Yield Monitor - Cursor Rules

## Project Context
This is an async Python application that monitors stablecoin yields hourly.
- Uses APScheduler for scheduling
- Collects data from DefiLlama API and individual protocol APIs
- Stores historical data in CSV files
- Sends reports via Telegram bot

## Code Style
- Use async/await for all I/O operations
- Type hints are mandatory (Pydantic models preferred)
- Follow PEP 8, max line length 100
- Use f-strings for formatting

## Architecture Patterns
- Collectors inherit from BaseCollector in src/collectors/base.py
- All data models are Pydantic models in src/models/
- Configuration via pydantic-settings from environment

## Key Dependencies
- aiohttp for HTTP requests
- APScheduler for scheduling
- python-telegram-bot for Telegram
- pandas for CSV operations

